<h2>2. Problem Definition</h2>
<p>
The most significant economic value of coastal regions worldwide is their capacity to attract global and domestic tourism. Tourism represents the premier global economic activity, creating critical foreign exchange revenue and fostering vast local employment opportunities across hospitality, transportation, and recreation. 
</p>
<p>
Prior to <strong>BeautyOfBeaches</strong>, travel portals targeting Pakistan's 1,050 km coastline and international coastal destinations suffered from severe deficiencies: fragmented information, lack of transparent local currency pricing in Pakistani Rupees (PKR), absent real-time marine and weather tracking, disjointed transportation logistics along the Makran Coastal Highway, and missing offline documentation (dossiers, downloadable travel guides, and verifiable payment receipts). 
</p>
<p>
<strong>BeautyOfBeaches</strong> solves these pain points by offering a unified, responsive Single-Page-Architecture website providing comprehensive beach destination intelligence categorized by four distinct geographical zones (WEST, NORTH, EAST, and SOUTH), integrated transit advertising (buses, flights, 4WD SUVs), live geolocation marine telemetry, and full PDF/DOC offline downloads.
</p>

<h2>3. Assumptions Made</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Target Devices &amp; Display Standards:</strong> The application assumes access via contemporary devices including Apple Macbooks, 4K displays, Windows PCs, iPads/tablets, and mobile smartphones running evergreen web browsers (Chrome 110+, Edge 110+, Firefox 110+, Safari 16+).</li>
  <li><strong>Local Currency Standard:</strong> All financial figures, room fees, coach fares, and diving expeditions are assumed to operate transparently in Pakistani Rupees (PKR), eliminating hidden international exchange conversion overheads.</li>
  <li><strong>HTML5 Geolocation Fallback:</strong> If a user accesses the portal in an environment where GPS hardware or browser geolocation permissions are restricted, the continuous scrolling ticker gracefully defaults to the Arabian Sea coastal coordinates for Karachi and Hyderabad, Pakistan (24.86° N, 67.01° E).</li>
  <li><strong>Zero-Dependency Client-Side Offline Exports:</strong> PDF and Microsoft Word DOC generation operate directly in the client's browser using jsPDF with AutoTable and standards-compliant Word XML Blobs, ensuring instant downloads without external server latency.</li>
  <li><strong>Local Storage Resilience:</strong> User wishlist bookmarks, inquiry submissions, and feedback ratings persist seamlessly across sessions utilizing the HTML5 Web Storage API (localStorage).</li>
</ol>

<h2>4. Hardware &amp; Software Requirements</h2>
<h3>Hardware Specifications</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i3 / i5 / i7 or AMD Ryzen 3 / 5 / 7 or Apple Silicon (M1/M2/M3).</li>
  <li><strong>Memory (RAM):</strong> 4 GB minimum (8 GB or higher recommended for 4K video rendering).</li>
  <li><strong>Storage:</strong> 500 MB free hard drive / SSD space for full assets, media, and video caches.</li>
  <li><strong>Display:</strong> Color SVGA or High-DPI Retina Display (1024x768 minimum, optimized for 1920x1080 and above).</li>
  <li><strong>Input Devices:</strong> Standard keyboard, multi-touch trackpad or two-button optical mouse.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Software Specifications</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Operating System:</strong> Microsoft Windows 10/11, macOS Monterey/Sonoma, Linux Ubuntu 22.04+, or Android/iOS.</li>
  <li><strong>Core Web Technologies:</strong> HTML5 Semantic Markup, CSS3 with Custom Variables, JavaScript ES6+, Bootstrap 5.3.3.</li>
  <li><strong>Vector Animation &amp; Graphics:</strong> LottieFiles Surfing Preloader Engine (lottie-web 5.12.2), Font Awesome 6.5.1 Pro Iconography, Google Web Fonts (Playfair Display &amp; Plus Jakarta Sans).</li>
  <li><strong>Document Generation:</strong> jsPDF UMD 2.5.1, jsPDF AutoTable Plugin 3.8.2, Office XML Blob Exporter.</li>
  <li><strong>Supported Browsers:</strong> Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Mozilla Firefox, Apple Safari, Opera.</li>
</ul>

